.TH SHB-TRUST 1 "October 2026" "SecretHarbor 0.1.0" "SecretHarbor Manual"
.SH NAME
shb-trust \- Manage the advisory trusted process list (not yet enforced)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBshb trust <list|add|remove> [name]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Maintains an advisory list of trusted tools, MCP servers, and processes. Entries are metadata only and do not currently change sandbox enforcement.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
\fBadd\fR
Records a tool, executable, or MCP server as trusted in the advisory list (not yet enforced).
.TP
\fBlist\fR
Lists all processes and tools currently recognized as trusted in the project policy.
.TP
\fBremove\fR
Revokes trusted status from an agent or process.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
$ \fBshb trust list\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb trust add git\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb trust remove git\fR
.SH SEE ALSO
shb(1)
.SH WEBSITE
https://github.com/logn10/SecretHarbor
